    "seq": 29,
    "type": "agent_text",
    "text": "The baseline now has a mesh-verified peak stress. Here is where things stand before I propose the first look.\n\n**Baseline (Structural Steel, 20 N in -Y, 3 mm bend fillets)**\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Mass | 0.0398 kg |\n| Peak stress, coarse / fine mesh | 82.6 / 87.2 MPa (5.5% change, converged) |\n| Peak location | Inside bend fillet between the foot top and the left sloped web, mid-length, about 2 to 3 mm above the foot |\n| Safety factor (required 1.5, default) | 2.87 on the converged peak |\n| Max deflection | 0.95 mm (fine mesh 0.95 mm) |\n| Reaction balance | 20.0 N, error 1.7e-6 (balances) |\n\nTwo notes:\n- The 2 mm fillet version could not be mesh-checked. Its halved mesh exceeded the Student node limit (136,064 nodes against 128,000). Using 3 mm fillets fixed this. The 3 mm result is the one I'm using.\n- Deflection: the baseline is about 1.0 mm, so the 1.0 mm cap I set earlier would already be exceeded. I'm changing the default to **1.5 mm** at the load hole. Tell me if you want it tighter.\n\n**Limits I'm using (defaults, you can change them)**\n- Safety factor \u2265 1.5 (the default you approved). This is the binding stress limit.\n- Max deflection \u2264 1.5 mm.\n\n**Proposed first look: minimise mass**\n\nFeatures I'd vary, one at a time, around the baseline. All bend fillets stay at 3 mm.\n\n| Feature | Low | High | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Foot thickness (top face offset) | -0.4 mm | +0.3 mm | Foot carries the bolt clamp and the bend stress |\n| Web thickness (left sloped web face offset) | -0.4 mm | +0.3 mm | Web carries the load from the hole to the foot |\n| Flange thickness (top face offset) | -0.5 mm | +0.3 mm | Flange holds the cable hole |\n| Big hole radius | 4.0 mm | 6.5 mm | Less material around the hole, but more bearing stress |\n\n- **Solves:** 2 \u00d7 4 + 1 = 9 designs.\n- **Estimated time:** 9 \u00d7 about 27 s \u2248 4 minutes.\n- Values from this screen are indicative only, not mesh-checked, and a one-at-a-time screen cannot show interactions between features.\n\nDo you want me to run this first look with these features and limits? Or would you change any feature, range or limit first?"
